{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/79604-janus-worshipping-hunters","id":79604,"title":"Janus worshipping hunters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-25T13:45:46-08:00","id":79604,"title":"Janus worshipping hunters?","content":"Where might one find more information on the Ianus-worshipping conspiracy found <i>Deamcatchers</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T14:09:23-08:00","id":79625,"title":"","content":"Take a Like just for having read Dream Catchers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sadly, there's not much more information about them. Glamourweaver came up with the idea but never wrote them, I put them in Dream Catchers because:<br /> 1) I like putting in little references like that. (There's two more non-Dream Catchers Fae-Conspiracies hidden in the PDF; one is REALLY subtle)<br /> 2) I felt that they'd make a good example, they know about Hedge navigation while being closer to a typical Hunter than the Wilde Society, and don't have a Hollow like the Sons that they could use to avoid the danger.<br /> <br /> <br /> Their proper name is The Staff of Janus, they're also known as The Gatekeepers.<br /> <br /> I think Glamourweaver described them as The Freemasons, if they were run by neo-pagans. A mixture of librarians, gardeners, academics and people with lots of money, they have power over time and doorways which they use to try and prevent travel between the worlds.<br /> <br /> Here's a <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?539058-HtV-but-knowledge-not-required-Need-help-naming-organizations\" target=\"_blank\">thread</a> with some discussion, I know there was a parallel thread on the white wolf forums but I can't find it anymore. I also made a basic attempt to think up some Endowments for them <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default3cb4.html?g=posts&amp;t=71224\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-20-2014, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T15:04:20-08:00","id":79676,"title":"","content":"Thank you, King's Raven. The additional details are much appreciated.<br /> <br /> It's a shame they were never finished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T22:09:04-08:00","id":79980,"title":"","content":"They never really conceptually developed. But feel free to play with the ideas we had. I think I landed on them being too much like the Order of the Knights of Saint George (charitable fraternal order to the public, actually a mystery cult trying to keep out dangerous divine forces)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T09:29:32-08:00","id":80292,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what to do about the similarity to the Knights of Saint George; perhaps their &quot;cover&quot; identity could be changed slightly? As I understand, the Masons evolved from actual trade guilds of masons (stonecutters/builders). You could put the Staff of Janus a little further back in this process, so that new members join what they think is an antiquarian gardening club/landscapers association (which would explain the number of gardeners and scholars in their ranks) before learning the truth.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here is possible set of factions:<br /> <b>The Grain </b>(like the grain of wood, not wheat): Their primary concern is simply closing doors that should never have been opened, followed by getting rid of the &quot;intruders&quot; who have already entered the world. Many of them believe that most monsters come from outside the world and that shutting all the gates into reality is the only way to stop the depredations of these creatures, whether by preventing further incursions or actual destroying the monsters by cutting them off from their home dimensions.<br /> <b>The Arch</b>: This faction believes some doorways serve a function as part of the &quot;architecture&quot; of the universe. By closing one door you may make it easier to open another by weakening the walls of reality nearby. On the other hand, an artificial gate may also cause structural weakness. This group decides very carefully whether to close gates, safeguard them, or even open new ones in the belief that mishandling could eventually cause the whole edifice to collapse.<br /> <b>The Keys</b>: This group, probably the smallest, believes that doorways exist to be used and merely attempt to decide who is worthy to use them. They also try to return things and people to their &quot;proper&quot; places, which means that it has the most infighting of the factions. Issues like whether changelings belong in Arcadia (being fae) or the mundane world (being originally human), or whether vampires should be sent to the Underworld with extreme prejudice are constant issues of debate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:20:09-08:00","id":80371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/79604-janus-worshipping-hunters?p=79625#post79625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take a Like just for having read Dream Catchers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sadly, there's not much more information about them. Glamourweaver came up with the idea but never wrote them, I put them in Dream Catchers because:<br /> 1) I like putting in little references like that. (There's two more non-Dream Catchers Fae-Conspiracies hidden in the PDF; one is REALLY subtle)</div> </div> </div> </div>great.. just great.. now I must find them or I won't be able to sleep at night.. thanks a lot :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T11:42:20-08:00","id":80400,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'll give you a couple of hints. First they've both got full write ups. Secondly they're both in fiction in Chapter Two. (Or I an tell you if you get tired of searching). Thirdly you don't see actually see members of the other Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> [edit: Also, looking again, I kinda screwed up on one of the two <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/79604-janus-worshipping-hunters?p=80292#post80292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what to do about the similarity to the Knights of Saint George; perhaps their &quot;cover&quot; identity could be changed slightly?</div> </div> </div> </div> My suggestion: Don't worry about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If what they're secretly doing is thematically and practically different to the knights, then it won't matter if they hide in similar ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/79604-janus-worshipping-hunters?p=80292#post80292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As I understand, the Masons evolved from actual trade guilds of masons (stonecutters/builders). You could put the Staff of Janus a little further back in this process, so that new members join what they think is an antiquarian gardening club/landscapers association (which would explain the number of gardeners and scholars in their ranks) before learning the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's how I saw it. Members think they're joining a charitable organisation with lots of networking opportunities and fancy dinners, for some that's all they'll ever see but if they have potential they'll be inducted to it's secrets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/79604-janus-worshipping-hunters?p=80292#post80292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, here is possible set of factions:</div> </div> </div> </div> Your names are awesome.<br /> <br /> My concern is that these groups feel opposed to each other. I can imagine the Grain trying to (or at least wanting to) destroy the Arch's and Keys protected doors. For some groups that's appropriate but I don't really feel it for the Staff. Instead I think that the each group should feel like part of a greater whole, much like the grain, arch and key of an actual door.<br /> <br /> So my thought would be that The Grain guard the door against improper use - of which 99% of use is improper. Using magic to seal the door and guns on anyone who gets past the magic.<br /> <br /> However on occasion - say at twilight on sunday on the last day of the month (god of liminality is an awesome concept) - then the door must be opened and rites to Janus must be performed. The Key guard doors when they are supposed to be opened, perform the rites, and make sure people/faeries only cross in the correct way. E.G. Maybe only intersex people should cross.<br /> <br /> For the Arch, I like your concept but I'm not sure how to fit it into this system. They should definitely feel like actual gardeners tending the supernatural landscape (or at least it's doors)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 02-26-2014, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T09:30:03-08:00","id":81633,"title":"","content":"I like your suggestions; it does feel like a group that shouldn't have a lot of internal conflict.<br /> Since both the Grain and the Keys seem to be focused on dealing with known doors, we could leave the Arch to find new ones and determine whether each is better off being sealed off permanently or guarded by the other two groups. To help them do this, the Arch's specialty could be Occult (Supernatural Doorways).<br /> The Keys might have Empathy (Personality) to help them judge who should be allowed to cross, but I'm not sure about the Grain. It would be nice to work gardening in somehow, but how would that help them in the Vigil? Maybe they should have a choice between Craft (Gardening) and Occult (Plants) so they would know the protective qualities of various woods, tying into their use of hawthorn in the original thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:24:10-08:00","id":81725,"title":"","content":"That sounds right for the Arch, gives a nice investigative focus to contrast the others. I like what you're doing with Keys, but maybe Occult (liminality) would cover the concept better. Finally Grain is good, it depends on the Endowments making use of those skills to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T07:54:58-08:00","id":82107,"title":"","content":"Now for some Stereotypes.<br /> <br /> <b>Les Mysteries:</b> They live on the borders and see the worlds as you only can when you live outside them; yet they would throw open the doors, tear down the walls and see us all become one. I suppose even clear sighted people can disagree, I have faith that in time our wisdom will be proven correct.<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b> First throw away the keys, then forget the gates exist, let the walls crumble down and put a thin line of armed guards in their place. How did those fools ever seize the crown?<br /> <br /> <b>Maiden's Blood Sisterhood:</b> After centuries of famine the old knowledge is returning in the most unlikely of places. Wait for understanding to bloom them welcome them into our garden.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">This one might require a little explanation. It's a reference both to the subtle hints of witchcraft/paganism in the MBS, and also to the fact that despite all attempts to change it, combat is still very much seen as a male profession. Therefore by being hunters and proudly female the MBS are a in a liminal space between the genders. A growth in the number of limnal pagan hunters is just the sort of thing to make the Staff feel happy. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Network Zero:</b> You can see much when you're outside of society, but without gates of wisdom your mind is open to weeds of misinformation.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not too satisfied with the Net0, but there's definitely potential in something about them being somewhat liminal due to being social outcasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T15:56:19-08:00","id":82818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/79604-janus-worshipping-hunters?p=82107#post82107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Network Zero:</b> You can see much when you're outside of society, but without gates of wisdom your mind is open to weeds of misinformation.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not too satisfied with the Net0, but there's definitely potential in something about them being somewhat liminal due to being social outcasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this?<br /> <br /> &quot;You open doors and gateways of knowledge and revelation, but you slam shut the doors on those who see beyond your ugly duckling facade.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T16:43:20-08:00","id":82838,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;ugly duckling facade&quot;; but my intent was to reverse the typical thing where steryotypes of Net0 insult their hygiene by making the Staff believe it's their youtube-commenter-social-skills that lets them see the truth; but at the same time critising them for lacking wisdom and judgement. Partly because anyone who disagrees with the Staff is by default lacking wisdom, partly because Net0 really are very short on both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T16:49:45-08:00","id":82840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/79604-janus-worshipping-hunters?p=82838#post82838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by &quot;ugly duckling facade&quot;; but my intent was to reverse the typical thing where steryotypes of Net0 insult their hygiene by making the Staff believe it's their youtube-commenter-social-skills that lets them see the truth; but at the same time critising them for lacking wisdom and judgement. Partly because anyone who disagrees with the Staff is by default lacking wisdom, partly because Net0 really are very short on both.</div> </div> </div> </div>It refers to your comment about them being social outcasts. It means that there are people who take them seriously, though they might disapprove of some of N-Zero's methods or lifestyles, but as you said, N-Zero lacks wisdom and judgement sometimes. Hence, they push away what might be good help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T16:04:36-08:00","id":83562,"title":"","content":"I felt like writing, so here's the first half of their history. They'll need a second one describing how they came to be a freemason like society.<br /> <br /> =================================<br /> <br /> Magic is found at the thresholds. It arises at dawn and dusk, it is found at the border between civilisation and barbarism, the one who is neither male nor female but something in-between wields it.<br /> <br /> Magic has all the danger of the threshold. It is familiar enough to tempt, but foreign enough to betray us. It is the time our world changes, and it is the door through which strangers enter for both good and for ill.<br /> <br /> But doors have gates, and gates have gatekeepers.<br /> <br /> The Gatekeepers began as a Roman mystery cult, merchants who travelled beyond the Empire and adopted the habits and ways of barbarians in the name of profit began to speak of wisdom that could only be seen by their unique point of view. They made their sacrifices to Janus, the god of transitions, gates, passages and time so that they might receive his blessing every time they walked through the gates. In time they began to incorporate rituals and beliefs from the foreigners they traded with, intentionally solidifying their position between Rome and the barbarians.<br /> <br /> The original Staff of Janus lasted over a century without ever accepting the supernatural, that all came later. After Christianity came to Rome and the old mystery cults were outlawed. Most of the Staff willingly renounced their membership, their religion was a trader's network that had suddenly become unprofitable. What remained was an echo chamber of the most devout believers,<br /> <br /> Now they could have fled beyond the Empire, they were rich merchants with the money to make a good life for themselves anywhere they pleased, but their theology was centred around being half way between Rome and foreigners. Unwilling to leave they instead began a ritual designed to split themselves into two people, one Roman, one foreign. With their animus stretched across continents they could blend into Christian Rome without abandoning their faith.<br /> <br /> It didn't work, neither did their next attempt, but they kept at it. Raiding their collection of myths and rituals, and their wealth, they tried ritual after ritual until one of them worked. Just not how they hoped it would happen. Half of the high priest was thrown outside of the world entirely, something else entered the world.<br /> <br /> Whatever else happened to the priest, one thing was clear. He now understood magic, he understood the doorways between the worlds that Janus kept, and he understood just how foolish he had been. Gathering his remaining cult he fled north, remaining ahead of Roman conquests teaching them of what the magic he learned, and the true way to honour Janus: By guarding doors like the one they had so inadvertently opened.<br /> <br /> <br /> A woman dressed in a Roman toga wears a mask of a bearded Greek philosopher on the front and back of her head (similar in appearance to Janus, but clearly a different guy). She holds a hawthorn staff wrapped with mistletoe, the head of the staff is carved into a symmetrical two-headed key.<br /> <br /> We stand between the earth and sky.<br /> We stand on the borders of the world.<br /> We built the gates.<br /> We hold the keys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T15:17:23-07:00","id":87767,"title":"","content":"Since I can't think of a good second part to the history I'll do this next.<br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b><br /> <br /> The Gatekeepers make one thing clear to every recruit. They are not heroes, they do not hunt monsters or rescue the innocent. They are gatekeepers, they guard the doors and peruse any illicit visitors. That's all they do.<br /> <br /> Central to the Gatekeeper's ideology is the idea of liminality. The Gatekeeper's are human, but they are humans who have adopted ideas, rituals and practices from beings who dwell beyond the world. They stand on the border between humanity and the other. This unique perspective gives the Staff, and the Staff alone, the wisdom to govern the gates and with it, the right to own and profit from the gates.<br /> <br /> Even if the Staff of Janus isn't as wise as they like to believe, they are not fools. They know that the creatures who use the gates are liminial beings in themselves. Changelings were once human before they were twisted, and still partly are. Werewolves can become a man or a wolf as they will. The Bound have passed through the gates and returned with something from the other side.<br /> <br /> So how do the Gatekeepers justify their unique rights and privileges when others are clearly more liminal? The answer is the kind of self centred thinking common to most human organisations. We are humans, and this is humanities' world. No matter how liminal a supernatural being is, it belongs in it's own world. Providing the monsters understand that then the Gatekeepers will have no problem with them, and will even be willing to form alliances, there is nothing untoward about a border having a guard on both ends. The wealth and influence the Staff can call upon to offer sweeteners has led to some stable and successful alliances.<br /> <br /> Of all the monsters it is the fae with whom the Gatekeepers have the longest history. Other monsters may travel between different realms, but none create new doors with the casual ease that faeries do. The Staff of Janus fears that if left unchecked the Fae could tear down the walls and let their world flood into ours, sowing madness and mayhem in it's wake. They wield both diplomacy and guns in their attempt to stem the fae's travel, but their belief that even Changelings should not be permitted to live upon Earth has made them few friends.<br /> <br /> After the fae The Staff of Janus concerns itself with Werewolves and the Bound. Werewolves have a lot with in common with the staff, both believe that the borders between this world and others must be maintained and both believe they uniquely have the duty and right to protect and own the doors, so naturally they hate each other. The Bound are a diverse lot, and many could agree with the Staff's mission but very few will agree that they are supposed to live in the Underworld. Nobody wants to live in the Underworld. Still The Bound rarely create new doors so the Staff takes a less hard-line view, there is some room for compromise and The Bound are so very bribeable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Structures</b><br /> <br /> The majority of Gatekeepers form <b>The Grain</b>. With a gun they guard the doors and peruse intruders into the world. With a watering can and sheers they shape the landscape, drawing on the protective power of plants to lock and seal the gates into the world.<br /> <i>Free Speciality: Crafts (Gardening) or Occult (Plants) </i><br /> <br /> When the time is right stewardship of a door passes from The Grain to <b>The Key</b>. For a limited time the gate is openend and, for the right sort, passage is permitted. The Key are diplomats who welcome guests and merchants who profit from trade, but they are also guards who keep out the wrong sort.<br /> <i>Free Speciality: Empathy (L</i>iminality)<br /> <br /> Supporting both The Grain and The Key is <b>The Arch</b>. Formed of investigators and scholars The Arch seeks out undiscovered gates and studies known doors. They assess the nature and danger of each, determining how much effort should be dedicated to keeping the door shut, and under what circumstances travel should be permitted.<br /> <i>Free Speciality: Investigation (Gates) or Occult (Gates) </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-07-2014, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T08:44:02-07:00","id":92813,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunters</b><br /> <br /> You didn\u2019t think much, at first, about the bricked-over archway in the basement of your new house. Once you moved in though, weird things started to happen. The milk kept disappearing, sometimes before the bottle had been opened. The cat somehow hung itself from the chandelier. No matter how many times you pulled the ivy off your bedroom window, it was back the next day. When you caught your landscapers trying to break in, you demanded to know what was going on \u2013 and they told you. Now you help them guard all the doorways, including the one you live over.<br /> <br /> You were looking for an edge at the office. There was rumour one of your peers was promoted because she was in the same club as your boss, so you thought there would be no harm in joining yourself. At worst your fingers would get a little dirty. Then you found out the club\u2019s \u201ccommunal garden\u201d is much bigger than it should be, and some of the exits don\u2019t exactly lead to Kansas. Even though you\u2019ve managed to trade your silence and help for that promotion you wanted, you\u2019re not happy. No one seems to know what happened to the woman who got promoted before you.<br /> <br /> Your college Latin club never had more than three members. So when one of your late-night meetings was interrupted by ominous chanting in your favourite language, you couldn\u2019t resist investigating. Unfortunately, the cultists you discovered decided a three-person sacrifice would be just the offering to give their master after summoning it to this dimension. If the Staff hadn\u2019t intervened to prevent the gate from being opened, you would all be worse than dead. After that, you\u2019ve been eager to offer the organization all the help you can \u2013 although you\u2019ve started to wonder, was saving your souls just an afterthought?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:24:04-07:00","id":93005,"title":"","content":"You never planned to get involved in the occult. You're a financier, you deal in cold hard cash, business opportunities. Though you won't say no to formal dinners and tax deductible donations. Then one day it happened, something disguised as a human made you a trade that was too good to be true, the beginning of a plan to get your soul. You didn't know what it was, but your gardener did. He told his superior, his superior told the priestess, and she told you. You're still in trouble, that <i>thing</i> was good at what it does, but you've got someone on your side. That's more than most people in your situation ever had.<br /> <br /> About a month after you finished probation at the library your boss showed you an honest to god secret passage filled with books, mostly in Latin. She taught you to the passcodes members will use, gave you a promotion, told you what books you should start with if you wanted to learn real magic, and promised that you would never work again if you told anyone. Being a librarian for a secret conspiracy is just like being a regular librarian, it still keeps you awake at night.<br /> <br /> You always thought the Worshipful Company of Gardeners haven't had anything to do with gardening since the medieval ages, but when they explained they employed a few just for tradition's sake it seemed reasonable enough. The pay was above average, the job was secure, and if you worked at it you could get a great deal from a bank or law firm at the dinners. Over time you overheard a little hear and there, until without quite knowing when it happened you realised you were part of a conspiracy with a basic understanding of what you were doing. So long as they don't ask you to do anything weirder than plant extra mistletoe you don't mind.<br /> <br /> You were part of an ancient Oxford drinking club. You were also secretly transsexual. Now you always thought those two facts were completely unrelated until the professor who chaired your club tapped you on the shoulder. One highly surreal journey later you returned to Earth in the body you'd always dreamed off, and all the paperwork had been taken care of. Your professor is getting rather old and needs somebody to replace him. On Monday you'll start learning how to secretly prepare people for a journey like your own, and learning who would suffer if they were exposed to The Gatekeeper's secrets.<br /> <br /> <b>Status</b><br /> <br /> In the Gatekeepers Status comes from .........<br /> <br /> O: Whether it's at the university, wall street or just a blue collar landscaping company the Gatekeeper's network of connections and back room deals has given you a leg up. Take a dot of Status applied to a completely mundane organisation in the financial, academic, gardening, museum or literacy world. <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">(I'm not a fan of the Endowment at zero dot style - it ruins opportunities for building the organisation's character)</span><br /> <br /> OOO: You've advanced beyond the front organisations and are dedicated to the Gatekeeper's sacred, secret, mission. You've been trained in the lore of gates and briefly travelled to at least two different realms. As a result of your focused education you can take the Unseen Sense merit applied to gates. Your sense is fine enough to tell when a gate opens or closes.<br /> <br /> OOOOO: You're recognised for your wisdom and successes, traits the Staff are keen to see in future generations. You are introduced to a three dot Retainer who will serve you loyally in exchange for the opportunity to observe and learn.<br /> <br /> <br /> With this, the only big thing missing is the Endowment. Any ideas? What about you Glamourweaver? I do like the idea of an Endowment where you actually landscape for long term effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-20-2014, 04:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T18:01:41-07:00","id":202512,"title":"","content":"I like the concept of a Janus-worshipping cult that focuses on gateways to WOD &quot;otherworlds&quot; and the Grain/Key/Arch structure is cool as well. Not so much a fan of the Freemason/gardener thing or their history.<br /> <br /> One idea that I can't seem to get out of my head is that the supernatural patron of the cult (that grants their Endowments) is the Gate, the Exarch of the Abyss from Mage: The Awakening. I wouldn't make this the default but I think its an interesting option. .<br /> <br /> . The Gate is a god of people trapped in liminal states. She guards the unknowable and maintains the border between reality and the Abyss. He's worshipped by a particular heresy in the Seers called the Secret Order of the Gate. The Secret Order believes in encouraging the Abyss enough to use it to oppress the Fallen World and keep magic away from it. However, they also regulate it so it doesn't fully devour everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Secret Order's inner doctrine speaks of the Serpent and the Tree. The Tree is the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Fallen_World\" target=\"_blank\">Fallen World</a>, growing from filth up to the Supernal Sky. The <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Celestial_Ladder?action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#ba0000\">Celestial Ladder</span></a> was inevitable; the Tree always climbs, using the smaller life within in to manifest that fecund desire. If it ever grew too tall, it would envelop the heavens in its unclean tendrils and choke existence to death. It must be pruned, dismembered, and hurt from time to time. The Exarchs did it when they cut down the Celestial Ladder, and the Gate does it still, with the blackest, sharpest blade of all: The Abyss. That's the anti-reality's purpose. It's the Serpent, Niddhog gnawing at the World Tree -- but it too must be restrained. The Serpent and the Tree live in symbiosis. Unbeing seeks being, and devours it. Being fills the void until it's either stopped, or suffocates </div> </div> </div>. <br /> <br /> ...and I just realized how this also fits with the gardening aspect you have. Weird...anyways, t<span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">he <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Secret Order believes in two paths of service: the Opening </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Way and the Warding Way. Openers summon Abyssal manifestations; Warders banish them. You could tie this in to Janus' role as the two-faced god of beginnings and endings. Have the cult split into those two factions with the Openers using the gateways and acting as tradesmen while the Warders guard and lock the doors. </span>And hey, what's the name for another heresy in the Seers that worships the Gate? <i>The Gatekeepers.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call me Count <img src=\"images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2713-123456789blaaa","name":"123456789blaaa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T00:51:24-07:00","id":202726,"title":"","content":"The problem with making the Staff align primarally with Mage is that it's the least liminal of all gamelines. Changelings are half human, half fae. Werewolves are half flesh, half spirit. Sin-Eaters are half human, half Geist. Mage doesn't have that, nor does it have many gates for the Staff to guard. Mages are closest aligned to the astral, but there's no such thing as an actual gate to the astral realm.<br /> <br /> Even the Gate. She is Liminal, but from the Staff's perspective the Gate is closer to some &quot;anti-liminal benig&quot;. To the staff the point of liminality is that you have one foot in both worlds, and that only a liminal person can achieve the wisdom necessary to govern who should be aloud to pass through who should not. The Gate is liminal, but his whole purpose is to keep the universe the way it is, to maintain the Exarch's dominion. She's not well suited for a god of change: You'll notice that quote block mentions pruning back the tree, but it never mentions actually encouraging growth - just pruning and making sure Niddhog doesn't prune too much.<br /> <br /> The Staff are gardeners, to do their work without encouraging growth is anthema.<br /> <br /> <br /> In Mage terms, the Staff of Janus are much closer aligned to the Guardians of the Veil than the Seers of the Throne. They keep mortals away from the mysteries &quot;for their own good&quot;, but they also hand the mysteries out to the &quot;worthy&quot;, piece by piece as they are &quot;ready&quot; for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the freemason stuff is awesome...<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/202946-the-staff-of-janus-the-gatekeepers\">I should just finish them up. There's not much left to do anyway.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-20-2014, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}